WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.468
A remark by China's ambassador

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.435
to France has sparked

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.170
controversy right around the world

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.306
during a French TV interview.

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.741
Ambassador Lu Shaye

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:08.808
seemingly questioned

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.243
the sovereignty of former

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:11.611
Soviet republics.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.812
Now those nations

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.281
and you want answers from Beijing.

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:16.950
Lucia said this.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.852
These ex-Soviet countries

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.687
don't have an effective status

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.122
in international law

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:22.622
because there

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.657
was no international agreement

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.292
to materialize their status

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.461
as sovereign countries do.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:29.462
Chase Common said now.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.964
One of the topics at today's

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.699
meeting of EU foreign ministers

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:33.266
and it could

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.868
jeopardize China's efforts

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:35.935
to be a mediator

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.904
between Ukraine and Russia.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:41.041
Ivan Watson, extended all

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.409
comments by China's

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:45.512
ambassador to Paris on French television.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:48.181
Claims that former Soviet republics

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.383
don't have any real status.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.452
According to international law.

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:53.920
They triggered somewhat

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.922
of a diplomatic firestorm

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:56.823
in Europe

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.426
with the governments of three former

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:00.560
Soviet republics,

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.095
Lithuania, Latvia and Estonia,

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.830
all saying that they would be summoning

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.864
Chinese diplomats

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.700
to try to clarify these claims.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:08.601
And meanwhile,

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.203
a statement has come out

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:13.006
on the Chinese embassy in France's

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.941
website today,

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:18.411
showing a pretty sharp 180 degree U-turn

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:20.280
with the statement, quote,

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.114
The ambassador,

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:22.148
Lucia's remarks on

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.116
the question of Ukraine

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.851
were not a statement of policy,

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:25.718
but an expression

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.120
of his personal opinion.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.488
They should not be the subject

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:30.356
of over interpretation.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:31.324
And going on to say that

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.225
China

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:33.526
respects the sovereignty,

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.562
independence and territorial integrity

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:36.696
of all countries

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:39.632
and that China would like to help mediate

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:43.069
a peaceful settlement to Russia's ongoing

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:46.673
invasion and occupation of Ukraine.

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:47.440
But it appears

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.509
the damage has already been done.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:51.945
The Foreign Ministry of Lithuania says

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:53.046
his government

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:53.580
simply does

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.282
not trust China to negotiate

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.584
when it comes to this conflict.

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:58.585
Take a listen.

00:01:58.585 --> 00:01:59.419
This is a narrative

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:01.588
that we've been hearing from Moscow,

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:03.923
and now it's being sent out by another

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:04.824
by another country,

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.092
which is in our eyes

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.594
as an ally of Moscow.

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.429
In many cases, if not militarily

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:10.864
and politically at least,

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.800
and sending the same messages,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.502
questioning of,

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:16.703
you know, of the whole concept

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.571
of independence, of sovereignty,

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:20.840
which is very dangerous in these days.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:22.609
There have also been statements

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:23.643
by the European

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.111
Union foreign policy chief

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:27.647
calling the Chinese ambassador's remarks

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:30.416
unacceptable, also from another former

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.484
Soviet republic,

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:33.553
Moldova, its foreign ministry, saying

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:34.687
it was surprised

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:37.457
it wanted clarification from Beijing.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:38.024
Part of

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.226
this gets to the suspicion

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.761
in parts of Eastern Europe

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:42.962
about China,

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.064
which professes to be neutral

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.267
in the Russia-Ukraine war,

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.368
even as the Chinese

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.537
leader, Xi Jinping, continues to conduct

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:51.938
face to face meetings

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.573
with the Russian president,

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:55.108
Vladimir Putin.

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.109
While he has yet

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:58.111
to have any direct communication

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.579
with the Ukrainian president,

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.080
Volodymyr Zelensky.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.349
Ivan Watson, CNN, Hong Kong.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.951
Now in more dangerous place

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.152
than during the Cold War,

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.221
that is the worldview of Russia's

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:08.922
foreign minister,

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:11.057
who's been chairing a meeting at the U.N.

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:11.925
Security Council

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:14.027
over the past couple of hours, in fact.

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:15.328
Russia currently holds

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.363
the rotating monthly presidency

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.532
of the Security Council

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:21.034
as the session got underway.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:21.534
The U.N.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.902
secretary general slammed

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.637
Russia's invasion of Ukraine,

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.106
as well as the devastation it has caused.

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:29.042
In turn, Sergei Lavrov,

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.577
the man you're looking on your screen.

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:31.945
Said The world is currently

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:33.613
in a more precarious situation

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:34.981
than in decades. This is what he said.

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:37.350
As was the case

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:37.450
in the

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:37.917
Cold War,

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.285
we have reached a dangerous, possibly

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:41.221
even more dangerous threshold.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.822
The situation is worsened

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:43.690
with the loss of trust

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.857
in multilateralism.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.059
When the financial economic

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.126
aggression of the West

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.962
is destroying

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.530
the benefits of globalization,

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.798
when the United States and its allies

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:52.966
are abandoning diplomacy

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:55.034
in Japan, demanding

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:56.202
clarification of relations

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:57.337
on the battlefield

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:58.571
and this is all done in the halls

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.073
of the United Nations,

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:00.907
which was created

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:03.443
to prevent the horrors of war.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:04.644
Let's get more into this.

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.279
Richard Roth has the very latest

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.547
on the meeting from the U.N.

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:08.748
Richard, good to see you.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:09.983
I mean, what we heard there,

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.217
just a little clip from Sergei

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:13.686
Lavrov was a pretty less

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.288
long list of grievances,

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:17.023
but any acceptance to the

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:18.358
role it's playing in Ukraine,

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.893
acceptance by the other

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:22.395
members of the Security Council?

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:23.096
Not really.

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:23.596
I mean,

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:24.464
Sergei Lavrov,

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:25.365
the Russian foreign minister,

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.400
he was here for years as Russia's U.N.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.201
ambassador.

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:29.202
He knows the terrain.

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:30.003
He knew the storm.

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.771
He was walking into the U.S.

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:32.872
ambassador to the U.N.,

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:33.906
Linda Thomas-Greenfield,

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.375
before the meeting said

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:37.644
Russia is the giant elephant in the room.

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:38.578
It's still amazing

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.545
that there's a conflict

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.513
with one

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.948
permanent member of the Security Council

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.449
invading another country.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.450
And they are now

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.185
chairing the Security Council

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.121
for the month of April.

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:49.656
Lavrov will be present tomorrow

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:51.391
for another meeting on the Middle East,

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:52.825
and he'll be in the chair seat.

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:53.359
And he may hold

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:55.561
a press conference tomorrow The U.S.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:57.597
ambassador announced once again

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:59.866
Russia's actions are illegal,

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:01.501
trying to invade and take over

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.436
another member country.

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:04.637
A different note.

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:05.571
Elizabeth Whalen,

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.740
the sister of imprisoned U.S.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.408
citizen Paul

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:09.042
Whalen,

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:10.610
spoke to the press outside

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.211
of the Security Council,

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.546
and she defiantly said

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:14.914
that the US must help

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:16.416
get Whalen out of Russia

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:18.051
and Moscow must acquiesce

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.321
Russia's less than

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:23.256
sophisticated take on diplomacy

00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:25.191
is to arbitrarily detained

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:26.492
American citizens

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.795
in order to extract concessions

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:30.630
from the United States.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.398
This is not the work of a mature

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.067
and responsible nation.

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.302
It is the action of a terrorist state.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.572
And I am here to tell Russia

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:43.242
free paul whelan,

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:43.843
the u.s.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:46.412
ambassador, said that we ilin

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.047
and the Wall Street Journal reporter

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:48.614
Garrett scavenge

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.850
are political pawns in this matter.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:51.451
The u.s.

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:53.119
has spoken already at this meeting.

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.220
Russia has spoken, though

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.188
it's very possible

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:56.589
russia will want to respond

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:57.824
to all the criticism

00:05:57.824 --> 00:05:59.292
from major western countries

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:00.660
and some african countries

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.928
at the meeting.

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:03.596
Thank you very much,

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:05.131
richard roth for us there in new York.

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:06.132
Appreciate it, Richard.

